{"tool_name":"iedb-ar","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"iedb-ar","home":"http://tools.immuneepitope.org","summary":"The Immune Epitope Database Analysis Resource (IEDB-AR) is a collection of tools for the prediction and analysis of immune epitopes. Tools include B-cell and T-cell epitope prediction and epitope analysis tools. peptide:MHC-I binding and T-cell epitope tools have been added, mapping of discontinuous epitopes onto 3D structures was also added.","addition_date":"2017-02-14T09:36:02Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:53Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:iedb-ar","credit":[{"email":"help@iedb.org","name":"IEDB Support","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"http://tools.immuneepitope.org/main/tools-api/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Epitope mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0416"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2429"}]}],"name":"IEDB-AR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"The immune epitope database analysis resource (IEDB-AR: http://tools.iedb.org) is a collection of tools for prediction and analysis of molecular targets of T-and B-cell immune responses (i.e. epitopes). Since its last publication in the NAR webserver issue in 2008, a new generation of peptide:MHC binding and T-cell epitope predictive tools have been added. As validated by different labs and in the first international competition for predicting peptide:MHC-I binding, their predictive performances have improved considerably. In addition, a new B-cell epitope prediction tool was added, and the homology mapping tool was updated to enable mapping of discontinuous epitopes onto 3D structures. Furthermore, to serve a wider range of users, the number of ways in which IEDB-AR can be accessed has been expanded. Specifically, the predictive tools can be programmatically accessed using a web interface and can also be downloaded as software packages. \u00a9 2012 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Bourne P.E."},{"name":"Greenbaum J."},{"name":"Kim Y."},{"name":"Lund O."},{"name":"Lundegaard C."},{"name":"Nielsen M."},{"name":"Peters B."},{"name":"Ponomarenko J."},{"name":"Sette A."},{"name":"Tamang D."},{"name":"Wang P."},{"name":"Zhu Z."}],"citationCount":274,"date":"2012-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"Immune epitope database analysis resource"},"pmid":"22610854"},{"metadata":{"abstract":"We present a new release of the immune epitope database analysis resource (IEDB-AR, http://tools.immuneepitope.org), a repository of web-based tools for the prediction and analysis of immune epitopes. New functionalities have been added to most of the previously implemented tools, and a total of eight new tools were added, including two B-cell epitope prediction tools, four T-cell epitope prediction tools and two analysis tools.","authors":[{"name":"Beaver J."},{"name":"Bourne P.E."},{"name":"Bui H.H."},{"name":"Buus S."},{"name":"Frankild S."},{"name":"Greenbaum J."},{"name":"Haste-Andersen P."},{"name":"Kim Y."},{"name":"Lund O."},{"name":"Lundegaard C."},{"name":"Nielsen M."},{"name":"Peters B."},{"name":"Ponomarenko J."},{"name":"Sette A."},{"name":"Wang P."},{"name":"Zhang Q."},{"name":"Zhu Z."}],"citationCount":215,"date":"2008-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic acids research","title":"Immune epitope database analysis resource (IEDB-AR)."},"pmid":"18515843"}],"topic":[{"term":"Immunoproteins, genes and antigens","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2830"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0081"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotoo